  "finalText": "Fixing the phrase 2 exit timing; now checking the transitions.\nThe quote is built as a 4-phrase, 8 s piece on a dark background. I checked it in a contact sheet, and the phrases hand off to each other without stacking up.\n\n1. **\"Design is not\"** (0–2.2 s): off-white bold type, slides in word by word (Expo Out), then lifts and fades out.\n2. **\"just what / it looks like.\"** (1.9–4.3 s): lighter weight, grey, so it reads as secondary. It arrives while phrase 1 is leaving, then exits upward.\n3. **\"Design is\"** (4.0–5.8 s): bold, drops in letter by letter. It then glides up to become a header.\n4. **\"how it works.\"** (5.4 s on): 230 px, weight 900, orange (#FF5A1F). It pops in per letter with a springy overshoot and is much bigger than anything else.\n5. **\"— STEVE JOBS\"** (7.0 s): small, tracked-out and grey. It fades in last.\n\nAt 4.1 s the incoming \"Design is\" briefly overlaps the end of the phrase 2 exit. It is brief and reads as a crossfade, but I can move the entrance later if you'd rather have a cleaner gap.\n\nI can add a subtle camera push or a loop-friendly ending if you want. I can also try a tighter, faster version for social."
